 "struct_currency_removed": "owner, 2026-11-12: no redundant dimensions. The allocation's structural dimension named currency (dim_id 8) was labelled by a character check, a value holding $, the pound or the euro sign (training/props/build_assignment21_v2.py); the new engine's sheet compiler reads that from the cell's format and symbol as a fact, so no learned dimension holds it. It is removed here and the schema.org property currency (the currency a monetary amount is expressed in) takes the name, as a taxonomy entry. Main's alloc.json, which describes the promoted 90-dimension model, changes at integration.",
 "structure_and_intent_removed": "owner, 2026-11-12: no redundant dimensions, so alloc.json holds only schema.org properties. The other 8 structural dimensions (is_str, is_num, num_frac, is_time, is_bool, is_enum, is_key, is_ref) and the 10 intent dimensions (intent_agg_count ... intent_limit) are removed with the warm-start map that named them: the new engine's sheet compiler states value kinds and column roles as facts, and its 100 closed structure names (engine/program/names.py, engine/sheet/names.py) carry aggregate, condition and ranking, trained from compiler labels and gold programs; nothing in engine/named, engine/program, engine/sheet or training/named read them. dim_id is now the property's place in the basis, in the same order (the 71 were 9-82 and the additions 90-101). The promoted 90-dimension model on main and the old props pipeline (training/props/, training/taxonomy/) still use main's alloc.json, which changes at integration.",
